From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:42:22 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 198/207] dsv41 server: the compute default leaves a client's
 python to it; compute_executed counts runs

Under TF_DSV41_COMPUTE_LANE_DEFAULT=1 a request whose client offers its own
function named python was refused, though the client never asked for the
lane. A model's call carries only its tool's name, so two tools named
python cannot both be offered and have each call go to its owner, and
renaming the built-in would give the model an unmeasured prompt with two
near-identical tools to choose between. So under the default a client's
own python keeps the name: the built-in tool steps aside for that request
(the prompt is the client's own, nothing holds, its python calls go back
to it), while the runner's cells and guide stay on and
compute_executed still reports them. Only a request that lists
code_interpreter next to its own python is still refused, as it is with
the default off. A byte-equal copy of the built-in is still one
declaration.

compute_executed.calls counted the lane's reports, which include a call
with no code and calls past TF_DSV41_COMPUTE_LANE_MAX_CALLS that no
executor ran. It now counts the calls the circuit ran to its halt or the
sandbox started (Reply.compute_ran, not serialized), once a call under
verify; the reports themselves are unchanged. With the default unset
nothing changes: no counter, the same tools and the same reply bytes.
